This statement draws on factors of production and how businesses combine them. Treat it as a checklist against the core concept named in the stem, not as a general opinion about business.

In this setting, technology applied in production matters in services, not only factories. The wording matches the textbook relationship without adding extra conditions.

Every part of the claim aligns with the standard concept, so the statement stands.', 'FALSE — On the Fuhrmann definition used in the entrance exam, the sentence is false. Technology counts as a factor only where a firm manufactures physical hardware.

This statement draws on factors of production and how businesses combine them. Treat it as a checklist against the core concept named in the stem, not as a general opinion about business.

Applied to this claim, technology also matters in service businesses such as it support. That is why the sentence does not survive careful reading.

Once the overclaim or mislabel is exposed, the only consistent answer is false.', 'FALSE — The claim is false. Design know-how is capital because it is stored on servers.

The scenario is a worked example of factors of production and how businesses combine them. Translate the story into the textbook category first; only then judge whether the sentence describes that category accurately.

Applied to this claim, know-how applied to production is knowledge, not capital by storage medium. That is why the sentence does not survive careful reading.

